Glen,

For many DEC SCSI drives, the default is to spin up on command from
the SCSI host adapter.  Unlike other brands, the DEC drives keep this
information in some writable firmware-like storage read by the drive
at power up.  You can change the drive spin up by running the program
RZSPINUP.EXE in the MS-DOS world.  I have a copy, haven't run it yet,
and don't know exactly where I found it on the net.

Try doing an Alta Vista search for "RZSPINUP.EXE" on a web page
somewhere or an ftp search at http://ftpsearch.ntnu.no to check thru
the ftp archives of the world... Ben Myers

