You can try to open it and look for a Vertical Lineary pot  (might  be
labeled V-LIN or something). If you're a daring sould, you can try  to
adjust it WITH A PLASTIC SCREWDRIVER and taking all precations not  to
get  an  electric shock. Don't sue me of you do. I warned you, this is
dangerous, but I've fixed several VR262's like that.

Unfortunately,  this  is  usually  a  sign  of  the  deflection  board
approaching  its end of life. Those VR262's were short-lived beasts. I
have a pile of those with burnt deflection boards.

Good luck,
