I am wondering how other sites assure the time is the same on all VAX 
nodes on the network.  We have two VAX 6610's and ten VAX 4105's and 
various other smaller VAX's on our plantwide network.  Currently we use 
a RS232 signal from a WWV reciever and some internal written custom 
software to set one of the node's time.  There is another piece of 
custom software running on all the other VAX nodes to set their time 
from the "master server".  We do not run TCP/IP on any of the nodes.  I 
have found various NTP-TCP/IP servers on the markets.  The WWV port and 
information is sometimes unreliable.  Any suggestions would be 
appreciated.  Thanks in advance.

