Has anyone else experienced such horrible customer service? I contacted Digital for 
assistance when my system was hanging up just prior to going into Windows. 

I was charged $40 for phone assistance.  This was only the second time I had ever called 
with a question.  I purchased $5K and my parents another $5K worth of Digital equipment. 
Only a measly $10,000.00  But they cannot spare the cost of supporting their customers! 
Often busy people don't have enough time on the computers when they first buy them to 
even need help. They add insult to injury when the fault of the error turned out NOT to 
be a software error of ours after all but their motherboard crashing.

Anyhow, when I called, I was able to get into Windows but the system was extremely slow. 
By the time I finished with the customer service rep. my computer brought up a black 
screen and halted.  I had done most of the things she instructed me to do before I had 
called.  But she insisted on reading word-for-word out of a book to me.  She would not 
hear what I was trying to tell her -- nor was she interested in troubleshooting the 
problem.  At this point she simply told me to re-format my hard-drive and bailed out.  I 
would have to pay another $40 to get help again!  

When my husband and I called customer service again to get a tech to come out and look 
at it (we purchased extended warranty) once again, tech "support" did not want to "hear" 
what we were trying to convey to them.  Upon asking for a Supervisor, we received more 
incompetence and the final person to handle our call could not even keep their data 
entry screen up to assist us.  "Oops, how does that happen" she said as she wiped out 
our data from the screen and wanted us to re-iterate everything.  The data passed across 
a room was not even relayed efficiently enough for the final tech to have it 
as well. "Oh, I don't have your data here".  "Whom did you talk to?" She had to "walk 
around" to find out who had it, while we held the line.  Let's just say, it didn't give 
us any more confidence in Digital products.

Since reformatting my hard drive as a result of the first call, we found out our tape 
drive malfunctioned and we have lost everything - irretrieveably. Not only injured but 
insulted by their arrogant customer representatives.  It was unbelievable.

This is a warning to everyone else... BEWARE . . . if you buy Digital because of a 
supposed review of "four star" customer service, it just wasn't true -- at least in our 
case -- you may just end up like us!



