WinDX is (or was) an unreleased code translator that converted 16-bit 
Wintel binaries to Alpha format. T'was demonstrated way back in 1993, but 
never released because it required significant ISV and end-user 
intervention. DEC (rightfully) figured that nobody would want to get 
involved in such hassles.

So now the Big Question is, what will be the next source architecture that 
the Digital Semiconductor code translation specialists attempt to target?

