	You can buy just the motherboard and plug most of your existing
equipment, assuming it's fairly mainstream stuff (i.e. has Alpha
Drivers). If you're using non-parity RAM, you'll need to switch to
parity, as that's what the MB supports. Also, you need to bank the
memory in quads, rather than the pairs a Pentium requires. Get an ATX
case (and the elusive backplate that fits the motherboard) and you're
set. Good luck.

