time and of course on the type of machine.  Free would be best (and I
HAVE seen 3100s and even 4000s given away) but obviously if a new, fast
ALPHA with guarantee can be had for DM 9000 I wouldn't want to pay more
than a few hundred marks for a VAX or a couple of thousand for an ALPHA
(again, depending on the individual machine), which doesn't mean I could
necessarily fork out this much at any given time.  I could pick up the
machine by car anywhere in Britain, southern Scandinavia or on the
Continent north of the Alps except for France or the former eastern
countries. 

More details: at least 16 MB memory (32 for Alpha), at least 1GB SCSI
disk, all software and hardware installed and working (so I can
literally just plug it in and get to work; this is not important in the
long term but is right now).  A terminal is NOT a requirement but
wouldn't hurt; a VTxxx (or good emulation, such as FALCO) would be
perfectly sufficient.  A tape drive (EXABYTE or DAT) would be nice but
is not a requirement. 

