[ Birgitt Boersch-Pulm ]

>>  # ./interman -I tu0
>>  Colour display detected
>>  Page type: A4
>>  tu0: No such file or directory

I suspect that the problem is that either

(1) you don't have the packetfilter kernel option installed, or

(2) if it is installed, you haven't made the special files that
are needed.

If it's (1), a "doconfig" can be used to create a configuration
file which specifies that the packetfilter option be included.
Build a new kernel, and reboot.  (And do #2 below, too!)

If the packetfilter option *is* installed, then it's likely to
be problem (2):  Just do ...

        cd /dev
        ./MAKEDEV pf

... and you should be in business.

And if you've already done *both* those things, then I have no
other useful suggestions!

