The days of Digital developing IO boards and drivers are gone. 
My office is stacked with third party SCSI and network adapters. 
Qualification of multi-function adapters and drivers is high on 
my priority list. But just because you can find vendors saying 
they have boards that work on other platforms does not mean that 
they work on an AlphaServer. In doing options qualification on 
the 4100 we found several adapters did not work. The extremely 
high performance implementation of the dual PCI busses exposed 
the weakness in the board designs. Some vendors have even 
thanked us for debugging their design in our lab.

Our key concern is to insure the integrity of the customers data 
which demands extensive qualification efforts. Over the next 
several weeks/months spreading IO should be a much easier task. 
Scan the Supported Options List on the DIGITAL WEB pages for 
official information.

	Dennis Bak, AlphaServer 4100 Systems Engineer
	bak@poboxa.enet.dec.com



