I've been using one with a "normal" video card for several months with OS/2. A
couple of friends have also got them running with Linux and NT.

>What H./V.Sync frequenzies does VRT19 expect. Are these 
>frequencies fix?

The monitor is fixed frequency, only accepting 72Hz Vertical x 77KHz Horizontal
refresh at 1280x1024 resolution (though a friend got his running at 60Hz and 1600x
1200 resolution too).

You'll need to hack a monitor cable to get the horizontal and vertical sync
onto the green pin. Of course you'll only ever get a picture in graphics mode,
so all this can be a pain to setup.

Or, you can just go out and buy the correct video card to work with these
monitors, and then all modes, text and graphics, with work fine.

Goodluck,
Steven P.



