XTREEmist wrote:
>> Does Eudora allow me to do SET FILE mailfile? I have about 5 mail
>> files, with dozens of folders in each one and use lots of DEFINE/KEYs
>> to switch between them. MAIL.MAI is just one of them...

Nope - using standard POP3 on the server side, there is no way to do it
directly from Eudora. POP3 server usually reads the default mail file
(MAIL.MAI) and its folder NEWMAIL. The basic idea with Eudora is to make
users organize their folders on their local disks.

Some POP3 servers (e.g. MultiNet POP3) allow users to change the folder
which will be used by remote clients by defining logicals or symbols in
login procedure, but I don't think any of them permits changing mail file
or directory.

One of the ugly, but working solutions to this problem is to place mail
files in separate directories and changing MAIL_DIRECTORY parameter by
some external way (e.g. using telnet before reading mails by Eudora or
using some RSH-like commands).

Regards,
Beri
