Ron Natalie <ron@sensor.com> wrote:
>Terry C. Shannon wrote:
>
>> Nope. AXP, an acronym for nothing at all, was at one time used by DEC in
>> conjunction with the Alpha name. Seems to have fallen out of favor (note
>> that Alpha is now on its fifth or sixth logo!). Alpha is Alpha, AXP
>> suffix or no.
>
>My guess is that "alpha" is so heavily overused that it's impossible
>to get trademark registration on (hence the meaningless AXP).  

Very likely true. Alpha started out as the code name for the 
Son-of-PRISM/Son-of-EVAX processor architecture. Hence some wags claim 
that AXP stands for Almost eXactly Prism.

But you rarely see DEC referring to Alpha as AXP (or AXP's predecessor, 
Advanced RISC Architecture, a.k.a. ARA--and a.k.a. something quite nasty 
in a Middle Eastern language) these days.





