Since I started using the NEWSRDR program to read news, I look at the 
first article in each thread and then do a SET SEEN/ALL to ignore the 
rest of the thread or, if I'm interested, do a READ/NEW/THREAD to follow 
the thread.  (These and other common commands are of course defined in 
my keypad.)  At first, I missed the ability (which I don't think NEWSRDR 
offers) to go through the list of (threaded---NEWSRDR is threaded, of 
course) postings and select those I wish to read, until I realised that 
it's quicker to display a screen of the first post of each thread---with 
the possibility to glance at the contents if the subject line is not 
informative enough.

This gives me the advantage of being able to respond to spammings, out
of a sense of moral responsibility, before SETting the rest of the
THREAD SEEN and ignoring any followups etc.  I defined a key to forward
the post to the postmaster of the site (obtained from the
headers---usually I can see if they're faked), which pops me into EDT
where I have a key defined to include a standard letter of complaint.  I
usually put the spammer's address (just copied---I do it on an ASCII
terminal by pressing hold screen and then using the arrow, select,
remove and insert keys, but a mouse works as well, of course, if you're on
a graphic terminal---from the output of DIR/HEADERS; again, I can
usually see if it's fake) on the line as well.  Takes about 5 seconds
after a bit of practice.  Often, I get an email from the postmaster,
thanking me for the complaint, and informing me that the account has
been revoked.  When I don't get a reply from the postmaster, still many
of these spammers tend to disappear from the net, so I think that this
does really help to get rid of the spammers.  Like I say, just 5 seconds
and it does seem to help. 

