Yup, it does sound a lot like Andromeda (maybe the project name is more
than a coincidence).

Burns Fisher mentioned spinlock contention as a limiting factor in scaling
shared memory multiprocessing. If anyone is looking at that aspect, there
have been a couple of interesting projects (outside of Digital) dealing
with shared memory systems over less-than-backplane speed interconnects,
that have shown siginificant gains by special casing spinlock access (e.g.
aligning spinlocks within data structures and making the memory management
subsystem aware of a spinlock access vs accessing any random page). 

