>> In comp.os.vms Mark Honeycutt <mfhoneycutt@earthlink.net> wrote:
>> > I've got several RD53s for my MicroVAX II that I can't seem to get
>> > working. In the technical manual I have it mentions the four
>> > switches on the read-write board, but that the drive number is
>> > determined by position on the controller board. This works ok for
>> > my boot disk, DUA0. I am, however having problems with the other
>> > drives.

The drive number depends on 1) the jumpers/switches on the drive itself 
and sometimes 2) the distribution cable/panel/board used.

For example... when using the leprechaun boxes and two RD5x disks, the
DS3 line would be selected for both.  The cabling out of the boxes caused 
the DS4 line to be connected to DS3 on the second drive.  Even in many 
PCs, the disk cable had a twist in it in order to present the other disk 
select signal to the second disk, which would be configured identically 
to the first.

In the BA23 box, with pdp-11s and uVaxen, you could have two drives (I
have such a system).  The first drive is set for DS3... the second has to 
be set for DS4... there is no switching of signals between the 
distribution board and the connectors for the disks.  The other thing I 
found out for the BA23 box is that it has to have the front panel with 
six pushbuttons (instead of the typical four) for this to work, unless 
you are read to do some wiring or other jumpering (I know it is possible, 
but I don't know what has to be done... I just figured the easy way was 
to have the six-pushbutton panel).

So, what box are you trying to do this with?  And what do you have for a 
signal distribution board?

