  Re: to this and some of the other postings.


  First, the concept of Galaxies is a software architecture.  It is more, or less, useful
  depending on the underlying hardware that it is implemented on.  Existing "SMP" designs
  may or may not perform well, and they are no more relaiable hardware-wise (in particular
  memory errors and bus errors) than a monolithic SMP system.  That does not mean that
  future systems could not take advantage of the organization of a Galaxy to provide very
  high (in fact, non-stop-ever) reliability.

  Galaxies are using a design target of commercial databases and servers.  But if you look
  closely at it, you will notice that it also has application in many areas - including
  scientific/technical computing.

  Those of us working on the project are trying to contain ourselves and not try to answer
  everyones questions in a fragmentary way.  Expect a white paper on Galaxies in not too long,
  that should answer many of the questions you have, and more.

  The SGI box is really pretty cool from what I've read.  If they had OpenVMS and Galaxies -
  they'd be a world beater ;-)


_Fred



