If you want a price-performance comparison...

Look at Bapco's numbers for the Dell Dimension XPS Pro 200
and the 400 Mhz 21164 Alpha (www.bapco.com)

On Bapco's tests, the overall performance difference between
the Dell and Alpha is a hair over 1%. And at CAD, the Alpha wins
by 37%.

Then compare the prices of the Dell (check at www.dell.com) and
the Enorex 433e (at www.enorex.com).

I think you'll find that similarly configured systems are within
a few hundred bucks.

Of course the Enorex has only a meg of cache, whereas the
Bapco-tested Alpha had 2 megs. But then the Enorex runs at
433 Mhz to the 400 Mhz of the Bapco-tested Alpha.

For someone paying an engineer to do CAD work, the Alpha
system will quickly repay any price differece.

OTOH, if someone uses only Word, Excel, etc., then buy a
cheap Pentium.

