|> It surely is. It would require a 512bit wide bus running at over 1.4GHz.
No.  Whatever the number actually is, it isn't one bus or disk.  Whenever people
quote disk throughput numbers for big machines, they involve many disks
and channels, with at least the following interesting basic metrics:
	(1) 1 Thread read or write1 file [striped across disks]
	(2) Multiple threads read/write 1 file [striped across disks]
	(3) Multiple threads read/write many files
	(4) Multiple threads, but compute number of I/O operations, i.e.,
	an IOP throuput rather than a GB/s number.

