This isn't exactly a number crunching benchmark. Bapco is a business
application benchmark, and I don't think that anyone can deny that no
matter what you think about Microsoft, Excel, Word, and to some lesser
degree I suppose, PowerPoint, are the defacto application used by
businesses
so it would make some sense to use those applications as part of the
"business application benchmark".  Also, if I recall correctly, was it
not hashed out a while back that there aren't any more hand coded
assembly in Word or Excel? I recall that the claim was that it's now all
done in a high level language, then compiled to a psudo-code, then they
had platform specific compiler that took this psudo-code and compiled
it for the target platform.  I suppose that you can complain about the
relative efficiency of the different platform dependent p-code compiler,
as many have, but not about the hand coding business.

