agtabby@aol.com wrote:

> As stated in this this group already, if fx!32 allows you to run same
> speed as a pentium pro, why not just run pentium pro?  There is a reason
> to buy dec chips, if you have native apps in place.  Thus native nt apps
> appear to be still very necessary to allow alpha to succeed.

IMHO,  any of the following apps, all of which run native on Alpha NT,
is reason enough to favor Alpha over Intel.

     -Visual Reality
     -Real 3D
     -SoftImage
     -Autodesk AutoCAD

What I see now in the corporate environment is people running
AutoCAD, etc. on Intel because their management has an unreasoned
attraction to uniformity: The company wants everyone running NT.
NT=Intel. So you have to run AutoCAD on an Intel box.

I know that if I spent my days using AutoCAD or SoftImage, I'd
a lot rather have an Alpha box. With the sub-$3,000 21164PCs
coming along, price is not an issue. With Office available native
and  FX!32 making most Intel NT software available, then, in
many cases software isn't an issue, either.

If the software you use 75% of the time runs better on Intel NT,
then, by all means, run an Intel box

But if the software you use 75% runs much faster on a 21164PC,
and the Office apps and email you use the rest of the time run
fine, what's the point in going with Intel?

     -doug



