From what I know of the Galaxies Software Architecture, this would not be 
possible, at least initially. DEC has toyed with the idea of mixed-OS 
clusters but it apparently is a Great Undertaking. First off, a common 
file system would have to be developed. I've heard rumours that Spiralog 
may end up as a common DUNIX/OVMS file system, but these are just rumours 
and I wouldn't put much stock in them.

Secondly, the differences in reliability between DUNIX, OVMS, and WNT 
ensure that one of the OSes would be the weak link in such an aggregation.

Of course, when Spiralog is extended to support multiple clients (e.g. 
Unix and WNT), a Galaxies box could play a role as a back-end superserver 
to WNT and Unix clients.

This might make better sense than mixing OSes in a cabinet. After all, you 
put three OSes in a cabinet, you pay for three OS licenses!

Terry Shannon
Publisher, Shannon Knows DEC
shannon@world.std.com




