Yep... The 11/44 is 5 hex-height boards - M7904 data path, M7905 control, 
M7906 Multi-function Module, M7907 cache and M7908 Unibus Interface, 
along with a dual-height M7900 console interface module.

BTW, Am I correct (and most DEC manuals seem to agree) that 'height' is
how many subslots a board takes up (M7900 is dual height, M7800 is quad
height, etc), length is how far it sticks out from the backplane (say M105
vs M111) and Width is how many slots across a backplane it covers (most
modules are single-width, but some core memory modules take up 2 slots are
are called double-width). 

