connections to two remote sites using SLIP.  For one site, it is a very
noisy phone line, and for the second, we actually use a radio phone (
always going down ).  When the lines get noisy enough, the modems drop
the connection.  I am using cron scripts to monitor the status of and
restart the SLIP connections.  The machines I am connecting are Digital
AS600s running Digital Unix, and I am using a DECServer90TL terminal
server on the remote Alpha to control the modem.

My problem is this: about one out of every ten times the line is
dropped, the modem on the far end does not release the line.  It acts as
