Actually, both the DH-11 and the DHU-11 were Unibus.

A DHU-11 was a single card, while a DH-11 occupied an entire
"system unit" (i.e. it had its own backplane).  Programming details 
were different as well, so a DH-11 driver is, in general, different
than a DHU-11 driver.

The DHV-11 was the Q-bus version of the DHU-11.  Boards or options
often used a "V" or a "Q" to denote the fact that they were Q-bus.
(Though there are plenty of Unibus options with "V" or "Q" in their
name.)

Emulex made a Q-bus board called a "CS02" which could emulate a
DH-11 (an otherwise Unibus-only device).  This caused no end of confusion!

Tim "whad'ya mean, there's no Unibus map?" Shoppa (shoppa@triumf.ca)



