Charles Bouldin wrote:

> > I am running office 95 on my Alpha 21164 system onder NT4.0 using our
> > FX!32 software without problems. Blows the doors off my pentium...

> What speed is the Pentium that is having it's doors blown off? Does DEC have
> a web page describing FX!32?

There was an article on FX!32 in a recent BYTE
(Nov, I think).  It is a clever way of getting
around the legal implications of binary translation,
by isolating heavily used portions of translated
code into temporary dlls.  The speed-up over pure
interpreted code is noticed most at the second
invocation of a program (or an operation in a 
program).

The web info I've seen on FX!32 tends to be a little
hyperbolic.  The native version of Word on a 333 MHz
21164A with 4 MB L3 ran 9% slower than the native
version of word on a 200 MHz PPro, according to
the sysmark tests in BYTE last June; therefore some
of the claims should be taken with a grain of salt.

This from someone who wants to get a 21164pc system
next spring.



