In a previous article, nester@ad3100.ada.epa.gov wrote:
->We are having problems moving old mail files from our VMS mail to
->desktops running Eudora(PRO and Light).  Users can get all of their 
->"new" mail from the VAX using Eudora just fine, but they want to have 
->all of their old mail messages which are saved on the VAX to be 
->retrieved using Eudora also.  
-> 
->Is there a way to set the old messages on the VAX to allow Eudora 
->to think they are new again by changing a flag or attribute on the 
->old mail files?

Sure. Use VMS mail's "MOVE/ALL NEWMAIL" command to move them to the newmail
folder. Then Eudora will download them. Do this for each VMS mail folder and
you can reproduce the vms mail folder structure in Eudora by using a different
Eudora mailbox for each VMS folder.


