		#if defined(_OSF_SOURCE)


in previous versions it was;


		#if defined(_OSF_SOURCE) && !defined(__cplusplus)

	This prevents <sys/localedef.h> to be included and other

./sys header files, which are not necessary for C++ code builds.

Including results in redefinition for such compilers as GNU gcc and

libg++ libraries.

	In version 3.2 of OSF/1, the file has this restriction, maybe

someone did not know why?  Now you know the rest of the story.


