I'm not sure what you want to do.  If the 5/60 has an ethernet interface
(wanting tcp/ip) how can the terminal server help you?

We run from our axp host to our 5/25 floor PLC via their Pyramid
Integrator chassis.  It's essentially a stripped down 5/250 'next
generation' plc (just the resource manager).

It can have either an ethernet interface card installed (again needing
tcp/ip) and the interchange software, or a micro-vax. The u-vax has a
daughterboard integrated to talk to the back plane and thus the resource
manager, which switches the communications to DH+, the primary
communications network for allen bradly PLC's.

We use their interchange API calls for code written on the u-vax to
communicate the the plc.  Then use DMQ to communicate over decnet from
the host to the u-vax.

Mike Jensen



