What you need to do is issue a "isacfg -init" command from
the ">>>" prompt before attempting to boot Digital UNIX
V4.0. You need to be aware that "isacfg -init" will remove any devices you 
may have added optionally over the years. As a result, you will have to save
the information before issuing the "isacfg -init". 

The full procedure is documented in the release note for the platform which
can be found on the firmware CD or also at this location:

ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/Alpha/firmware/v3.7/doc/alpha200_v57_fw_relnote.txt

