As indicated by Megan Gentry, CoProcessor RSX and VAX-11/RSX are distinct 
products.  I don't know the support status of either, but I'd be very surprised
to find that CoProcessor RSX remained supported and available while VAX-11/RSX
did not.  VAX-11/RSX has been available since VMS V1, and was bundled with VMS
until VMS V4.  CoProcessor RSX came very late; I don't believe it achieved much
of a following as a result.  I thought there was an RT-11 variant that ran on
the KXJ-11 board, but Megan didn't mention it and she'd be one who would know.
The KXJ-11 is non-bus mastering (the VAX into which it is plugged is bus 
master), and so does not present itself as a normal PDP-11 to the operating
system.  If you had CoProcessor RSX (the KXJ-11 board plus the variant of RSX
that runs on it), I would think that RTEM would run on it.  However, the bus
mastering could be an issue.  Again, Megan would be one who would know.

/Jack
