In message <32839B1B.2BC5@interramp.com>, cd001837@interramp.com said:

  > I'm about to install a TZ30 in a MV 3100/95 and need to know the switch
  > definitions on the TZ30. There are 4 DIP switches labelled 1,2,3 and
  > 4. Any help is greatly appreciated. Thanks. Dave 
  
   I coincidentaly have a TZ30 service manual (EK-OTZ30-SV-001) here
  in which page 2-12 shows the following table.
  
              SCSI ID Switch Positions
  SCSI ID       4     3     2    1
  
     0          Off  Off   Off   On         Switch1 = Parity Bit (always
     1          On   Off   Off   On                   on ie Parity Enabled)
     2          Off  On    Off   On
     3          On   On    Off   On
     4          Off  Off   On    On
     5          On   Off   On    On
     6          Off  On    On    On
     7          On   On    On    On
     
  "SCSI ID = 5 is Standard ID for the TZ30 tape drive used in
  VAXStation 3100 systems."
  
  Hope this helps,
  
