: Thanks.

: Andrea Bertozzi

Great optimization on the f77 compiler. I have bench tested an
alphaserver 8400 (333 MHz chips) versus a power challenge
(194 MHz Mips R10000 chips). The alpha machine does one program
a tad faster than the SGI, whereas the SGI gives 30-40%
better performance on another program. Both programs
were f77 code involving a large fp workload but also quite
a lot of control statements that are probably difficult to
optimize. On the SGI I used the -O3, aggressive optimization
option and on the alpha I used the -fast and associated
options recommended by DEC. My assessment has been that the
Mips chip is probably potentially faster but the optimization
is not as good. Other workers I know have come to the same
conclusion.

Robert Bursill




