>Ah but FX!32 is _NOT_ an x86 emulator, it's a binary (JIT?) translator.

Please learn more about the technology before you assert
misinformation so emphatically.  FX!32 is both an interpreter and a
binary translator. It uses translated code where it is safe to do so.
It uses interpretation for correctness whenever it lacks translated
code or feels that the translated code cannot trust it.  For more
information see:

