In article <1996Nov7.223651.16695@decus>, geremin@decus.org.au (PDP-11 Trainee Guru) writes:
>:By the way, what do you know about RTEM, the RT-11 emulator for the 
>:VAX/VMS system? I am trying to get hold of a copy but cannot find anyone 
>:in DEC who has even heard of it. I want to run the RT-11 assembler and 
>:linker on a VAXstation-3100/38. Bloke up in NQ is interested, but I still 
>:have an SBC-11/21 here that I was thinking of putting on air again.

RTEM-11 provided the RT-11 environment on RSX and VMS systems, running
in compatibility mode on VMS, so you also need the RSX product for VMS.
I found I have a 1985 PDP-11 Systems and Options Catalog that lists
order codes QJ291-HM, HH, UZ and QJ304, and SPD number 30.21.xx.  These
order codes are the old style; the 291 and 304 are the unique product
identifiers.  Digital sold the RSX software several years ago; RTEM may
have gone with it.




