In article <3281C1F3.44C9@blkbox.com>, Brad <seq@blkbox.com> writes:
|>I've a brand new DEC 500 (333MHz, 256Mb).   Clicking on System
|>Information causes the system to crash.  I get "trap: invalid memory
|>read access from kernel mode"  Cause and solution?
|>

Cause:  you have a device on your system that has a "problem" with an ioctl
call issued by dxsysinfo when it probes the system for devices.  I suspect 
that the device driver of your graphics card is the culprit.  It would be
helpful if you could execute a 'sizer -gt' and provide the results.

Also, try to do (as root) 'file /dev/*'.  This will likely cause the same 
panic but the output could help pinpoint the problem device.

Unfortunately, I don't believe that there is any solution available at this
time.

Note that I have the same system but do not have the problem.  I assume we have
different graphics adapters.

