>If you don't have a 780, it's not going to do you much good.

Uh...no.

The hardware pdp11 instruction set exists on 11/750, 8600 and a few
others also. Besides that, a software emulator allows running pdp11
emulation on ANY VAX; comes with Vax/RSX.

Considering that some of the character instructions were handled by
emulators, this wasn't all that weird. A current architecture VAX
is probably better off than if the old hardware had been kept; the
same board, I heard, was used for pdp11 compat mode hardware on the
8600 that the 78x series had. The software emulator uses the native
instruction engine instead, which has sped up rather a lot over the
years. (It was supposedly built for speed, and uses considerable
space as a tradeoff.)



