We use a package called "conserver" we got from ftp.cc.purdue.edu (in /pucc).
We're running it on a couple of Sun IPCs with 8 port SBUS serial boards
to handle the consoles of a bunch of systems.  We have each console
in a separate xterm window.  The xterm window is the controlling console,
but you can login to the conserver system remotely and connect to the
console to reboot systems or see why it's not working.  It's saved a
trip into work more than once.


