In article <32763616.734C@student.dtu.dk>,
   Morten Kristensen <c898444@student.dtu.dk> wrote:
>I have recently purcased a MV3100-40. And I'm trying to get in contact
>with it. 
>I have tried to connect a VT100 terminal to the RS232 port on the back,
>but I don't get any thing on the screen. I'm using a null-modem.
>And now my question is, what am I doing wrong? Does anyone know about,
>how to "talk" with this machine? Please help me!
>
>Best regards,
>Morten.
O.K. Morten, I'll see what I can do.
First, if you are using a modem cable, (25 pin to 25 pin), this will not work 
for 2 reasons. 1) the computer and the terminal are both DTE devices, this is 
like connecting 2 terminals together. You need a 'NUL MODEM' device or cable 
to make this connection useful.
		2) This port is not the console. If VMS comes up and the port 
is not setup as a modem of printer port, with a nul modem cable you could then 
login on this port.
The console is the 1st 'Phone jack' MMJ socket on the left as you look at the 
back. (i think it has a '1' above it.) You will need a cable and 25pin 
adapter, nul modem connection to this to get to the console..
I am sure the system doesn't boot now as you don't have the ethernet connction 
terminated, this will make the computer stop on automatic boot at test 1
You will see this when you get the console connected as string like.

??1  XXXX.XXXX
>>>

You can then type a B and return, the system will then start.

Good luck!
(you are already lucky to have this machine!)



