letting their expensive box run pentium stuff.  This gives the
Alpha versatality:  a 25k box that will scream through native
apps, but still run x86 code fast enough to eliminate the need 
for a 3k pentium box (remember, you'd have to outfit the pentium
box with a huge hd and hi-buck monitor, but if the alpha emulates,
this stuff does double duty . . .).

I agree DEC cannot truly succeed until they get more native
