A kludge that might work if all that you need is to replace a VT100 at a 
remote site.
Obtain decserver(s) for each site which are capable of Reverse LAT
(decserver100,decserver90l+,etc are unsuitable).
On each decserver define a passworded (reverse LAT)service for the ports
attached to the console of the remote machine(s) .
Probably easier if port name is system name and decserver name is site name 
and the service offerred is the same to make things less complicated.

Then from a dumb terminal on a terminal server
Local> CONNECT console_svc NODE remote_site DESTINATION system_name
Password:

Not sure how this would work for a SET HOST/LAT session.

