> been set up incorrectly - can someone confirm this and possibly suggest
> some solutions ? A quick try with DEC support didn't get very far,
> either the printer was probably to blame, the network cabling or the
> DecNet setup depending on which department pass-the-buck. We don't want
> to call out an engineer for what could be a simple set-up problem.
> --
> Nick Ferrar

We are running around a dozen 17's, and found that the 16Mb is just
minimal.  We put an additional 16 in all and found it cleared up 
many of our problems.  They, though, were reported as VMerror (I think)
and pointed directly to memory exhaustion.

I would suggest always buying additional memory for the 17's.  They've
been good printers for us, but the 'os' that they are essentially running
does need a lot of memory.

As for setup, it is extremely sparse, and straight forward.  Very
little configuration to do at all.

As for the stalling, we have seen this with our printers, and a reboot
is the only thing that we were able to do as well.  It doesn't happen
with any regularity though.

So that's my two cents.



