Your numbers are somewhat out of date.  These 15 MB/sec.
drives are not exotic.  They are just fast 7200 RPM drives.
(e.g. Seagate  ST19171).

|> >Each individual disk has that max throughput, but
|> >the SCSI channel--and swapping, can move at up to 36M/s.
|> 
|> >Furthermore, disks often have hardware caches these days.
|> >Communication with the disk cache can be much quicker than
|> >the physical disk could support.
